        "Content": "For sale by Kelly Bradshaw via the iamsold Bidding Platform\r\n\r\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). For auction date and time please visit iamsold.ie. Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment.\r\n\r\n***INVESTMENT OPPORTUNITY / 5 FLATS / PRIME CITY CENTRE LOCATION / STRONG 11% YIELD***\r\n\r\nExceptional Residential Investment Opportunity – Period Property Over Four Floors \r\n\r\nSituated at 30 Summerhill Parade, North City Centre, Dublin 1 this impressive four-storey period property presents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial residential investment in one of Dublin’s most established and centrally located rental districts. \r\n\r\nThe property extends to approximately 214 sq.m. and comprises five self-contained flats arranged over four floors, including: \r\n\r\n•\t3 x One-Bedroom Flats  \r\n•\t2 x Two-Bedroom Flats  \r\n\r\nThe property was previously fully tenanted and produced a substantial annual rental income of approximately €75,888, demonstrating the strong income potential and long-term investment value of this exceptional asset. If one wants to further invest in the property, there is potential to achieve a higher yield.\r\n\r\nIdeally positioned in the heart of Dublin city, No. 30 enjoys an unbeatable location just moments from Croke Park and The Mater Hospital, while also being within comfortable walking distance of the city centre and the International Financial Services Centre (IFSC). \r\n\r\nThe convenience of this location cannot be overstated, with every conceivable amenity nearby including shops, cafés, restaurants, colleges, medical facilities, and recreational amenities.\r\n\r\nThe area is exceptionally well serviced by public transport, with numerous Dublin Bus routes, LUAS access, nearby Connolly Station, DART services, and excellent connectivity to the M1 and M50 motorways. \r\n\r\nThis is an outstanding opportunity for investors seeking a high-yielding, city-centre residential asset in a strong rental location with consistent tenant demand.\r\n\r\nFor virtual tour, copy and paste the below link:\r\nhttps://youtu.be/3g39FAggp_A?si=hn3dDXwHsiGhUUP7\r\n\r\nTo access the legal pack, please copy and paste the link below:\r\nhttp://www.iamsold.ie/properties/da32b92140424210827920d71ea9146f/auction-pack\r\n\r\nTO VIEW OR MAKE A BID Contact Kelly Bradshaw or iamsold, www.iamsold.ie\r\n\r\nStarting Bid and Reserve Price\r\n*Please note all properties are subject to a starting bid price and an undisclosed reserve. Both the starting bid and reserve price may be subject to change. Terms and conditions apply to the sale, which is powered by iamsold.\r\n\r\nAuctioneer's Comments\r\nThis property is offered for sale by unconditional auction. The successful bidder is required to pay a 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid. Please note this property is subject to an undisclosed reserve price. Terms and conditions apply to this sale.\r\n\r\nBuilding Energy Rating (BERs)\r\nBuilding Energy Rating (BERs) give information on how to make your home more energy efficient and reduce your energy costs. All properties bought, sold or rented require a BER. BERs carry ratings that compare the current energy efficiency and estimated costs of energy use with potential figures that a property could achieve. Potential figures are calculated by estimating what the energy efficiency and energy costs could be if energy saving measures were put in place. The rating measures the energy efficiency of your home using a grade from ‘A’ to ‘G’. An ‘A’ rating is the most efficient, while ‘G’ is the least efficient. The average efficiency grade to date is ‘D’. All properties are measured using the same calculations, so you can compare the energy efficiency of different properties."
